# Data files — what a pipeline writes when it is run from the repository root.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, so it applies to the root and nowhere else. The
# unanchored form swallowed every CSV and JSON in the tree, config files
# included, and had to grow a negation for each one that needed to stay — which
# is how frontend/package-lock.json went unversioned, leaving CI without the
# lockfile its 'npm ci' depends on. Anything committed on purpose, in
# tests/fixtures/ or frontend/, is no longer a special case to remember.
/*.csv
/*.json
/*.jsonl

# Frontend
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
# cod3s_data/observatory/static/ is deliberately NOT ignored: the built UI ships
# inside the wheel, so it has to be versioned. CI rebuilds it and fails if the
# committed artifact no longer matches the sources.

# Logs
*.log

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
